' Guide - one Retrofit request, end to end (explanatory diagram for the root README)
' Version 1.2 - 2026-10-20
' Example: opening Charizard's detail page. OkHttp and the Gson converter are what Retrofit uses
' under the hood; NetworkModule builds Retrofit with both. Hilt creates the objects once (@Singleton)
' and injects PokemonApi into PokemonRepository's constructor.
@startuml retrofit-request
!include ../style.puml

title Retrofit request - GET pokemon/charizard
autonumber

participant "Hilt\n(NetworkModule)" as Hilt
participant PokemonDetailViewModel
participant PokemonRepository
participant "PokemonApi\n(Retrofit proxy)" as PokemonApi
participant "OkHttp" as OkHttp
participant "Gson converter" as Gson
participant PokeAPI <<external>>

== Once, when Hilt first needs PokemonRepository ==
Hilt -> Hilt : OkHttpClient, then Retrofit\n(baseUrl https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/, Gson)
Hilt -> PokemonApi : retrofit.create(PokemonApi::class.java)
Hilt -> PokemonRepository : inject PokemonApi, CaughtPokemonDao

== Every request ==
PokemonDetailViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getPokemon("charizard")
PokemonRepository -> PokemonApi : getPokemon("charizard") (suspend)
PokemonApi -> OkHttp : GET /pokemon/charizard
OkHttp -> PokeAPI : HTTPS request
PokeAPI --> OkHttp : 200 OK, JSON
OkHttp --> PokemonApi : response body
PokemonApi -> Gson : JSON to Kotlin
Gson --> PokemonApi : PokemonDto(id, name, types, stats, sprites, ...)
PokemonApi --> PokemonRepository : PokemonDto (coroutine resumes on main)
PokemonRepository -> PokemonRepository : PokemonDto.toDomain() (data.mapper)
PokemonRepository --> PokemonDetailViewModel : Pokemon (domain model)

note over PokemonDetailViewModel, PokemonApi
  No network or HTTP error: the suspend call throws,
  PokemonDetailViewModel catches it and shows "No Pokemon found!".
end note
@enduml
